// 2+2W in the release-acquire fragment -- the SRA-vs-RA separating behaviour.
//
// rmm-zoo edge: SRA strictly weaker than RA is refuted by this; it is the
//               witness for the RA-vs-SRA ordering edge.
// Source: Lahav, Giannarakis & Vafeiadis, "Taming Release-Acquire Consistency"
//         (POPL 2016); Lahav & Boker, "What's Decidable about Causally
//         Consistent Shared Memory?" (TOPLAS 2022), Ex. 3.6.
//         Vendored shape: rmm-zoo litmus/strictly-weaker/SRA-vs-RA/2+2W.
//
// Each thread writes both locations and then reads the OTHER thread's write to
// the location it wrote second. Reading r0 = r1 = 1 forces mo to run against
// program order on both locations, closing a cycle in (hb u mo):
//   W(x,1) -po-> W(y,2) -mo-> W(y,1) -po-> W(x,2) -mo-> W(x,1).
// SRA's strong-write-coherence forbids that cycle. RA's write-coherence only
// forbids mo;hb, and neither mo step is followed by hb back to its source, so
// RA ALLOWS it.
//
// Reference verdicts: RA and WRA ALLOW. SRA and SC FORBID.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence allows, RC11 allows, RC17 allows, OD-LSO allows, RA
//     allows, SRA forbids, WRA allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z allows. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     MRD allows. RC11 allows it, and MRD is weaker than RC11 (zoo edge RC11 ->
//       MRD).
//     CC allows. Equivalent to WRA on the release-acquire fragment (zoo edge
//       WRA = CC).
//     Slow allows. Coherence allows it, and Slow is weaker.
//     Local allows. Slow allows it, and Local is weaker.
//   the models' definitions:
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: PC, PRAM, Causal,
//     POCausal, RYW, MR, WFR. C11 and C++17 are not implemented in MoRDor.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rel);
  y.store(2, rel);
  r0 := y.load(acq)
} ||| {
  y.store(1, rel);
  x.store(2, rel);
  r1 := x.load(acq)
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [Coherence, RC11, RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, MRD, RA, WRA,
                          CC, Slow, Local, MW]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, SRA]
